    {
      "data": {
        "text": "I have created the `embed_for_search.py` file in the current working directory with the following content:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModel\n\ndef embed_query(query):\n    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n    model = AutoModel.from_pretrained('sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n    inputs = tokenizer(query, return_tensors='pt', truncation=True, padding=True)\n    outputs = model(**inputs)\n    return outputs.last_hidden_state.mean(dim=1)\n\ndef embed_documents(documents):\n    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n    model = AutoModel.from_pretrained('sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n    embeddings = []\n    for doc in documents:\n        inputs = tokenizer(doc, return_tensors='pt', truncation=True, padding=True)\n        outputs = model(**inputs)\n        embeddings.append(outputs.last_hidden_state.mean(dim=1))\n    return embeddings\n```\n\nThis code uses the Hugging Face Transformers library to embed a query and documents for semantic search. The `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` model is used for embedding, making it identifiable as the external provider.",
